  "term": "gamma-hydroxybutyrate",
  "definition": "Gamma-hydroxybutyrate is a naturally occurring short-chain fatty acid found throughout the body, especially in the brain, where it acts on GHB receptors and to a lesser extent GABA-B receptors. It has neuromodulatory and anesthetic effects, mainly causing central nervous system depression.",
